1. Scope

This licence governs the EnigmaIS-owned myOwnCA software, accompanying release
verification tools, and documentation supplied with this licence (the
"Software"). It is a source-available licence, not an open-source licence.
Availability of source code permits inspection; it does not grant permission
to modify or redistribute the Software.

By exercising the permissions below, you agree to their conditions. Rights
that applicable law does not allow to be excluded or restricted are unaffected.
Third-party components are addressed separately in section 7.

2. Source inspection and noncommercial use

You may read and inspect the supplied source code. You may download, install,
run, and make necessary internal deployment and backup copies of unmodified
official releases for genuine noncommercial use, subject to this licence and
the product restrictions below. Keep copyright, licence, and attribution
notices intact. You may use the accompanying verification tools to authenticate
official EnigmaIS releases.

Noncommercial use includes personal projects, home labs, and education or
evaluation that is genuinely noncommercial. Use for the operation or benefit
of a business or commercial activity is commercial use. Evaluation for a
commercial deployment is also commercial use. Merely staying below a product
capacity limit does not make commercial use noncommercial.

The free myOwnCA allowance is 10 active certificate identities (lineages).
Genuine renewals, including key rotation, remain in the same identity slot.
Changing a certificate identity creates a new lineage. Imported external
certificates do not count toward this allowance.

3. Commercial use and customer licences

Every commercial use requires paid licensing terms agreed with EnigmaIS,
regardless of organisation size, deployment size, or certificate count. This
licence alone does not grant commercial use rights. Separately agreed written
commercial terms govern the additional permissions they expressly grant and
take precedence in the event of a conflict with this licence.

myOwnCA customer licence tokens are signed, installation-bound, and verified
offline. They record the recipient, installation, capacity, and validity period.
They must be used only for the authorised installation and under the agreed
terms. Possession of a token does not grant rights beyond those terms.

Renewal, revocation, CRL and OCSP generation, export, lifecycle monitoring,
notifications, audit, and recovery are not gated by paid certificate capacity.
Expiry or absence of a token does not itself grant permission for commercial
use, even if technical operations continue to function. The ability to run
software or issue a certificate is not evidence of a legal entitlement to do so.

4. Configuration, integration, and restrictions

Normal product settings, supported APIs, integrations through those APIs, and
deployment configuration are permitted within your authorised use. These
permissions do not permit changes to the application source or replacement of
its licensing or integrity controls. Your operational configuration, keys,
certificates, and database records are not EnigmaIS source code merely because
the Software creates or uses them.

Except as permitted by non-excludable applicable law or expressly authorised
by EnigmaIS in writing, you may not:

  - modify EnigmaIS source code or create derivative versions of the Software;
  - remove or bypass licensing, capacity, signature, or integrity controls;
  - forge, alter, or reuse customer licence tokens outside their authorised
    installation and terms;
  - remove or obscure ownership, copyright, licence, or attribution notices;
  - redistribute the Software to others, operate public mirrors, resell,
    sublicense, or offer hosted access to it without written authorisation.

These restrictions apply to both free and paid use unless separately agreed
written terms expressly provide otherwise. They do not restrict rights granted
by a third-party component's own licence.

